From: macos-local research
Subject: [PATCH] Give detached-heap temporary backing shareable host pages

Core creates a heap over temporary zero-filled storage before detaching it.
Linux address reservations are anonymous and cannot be remapped through the
file-backed alias table. Request shareable storage only for this backing;
keep ordinary reservations and remap failure semantics unchanged.

